			<div class="content" id="post-content-3592170">
									

<p>I'm left feeling a tad let down. I mean, &quot;unexpectedly ramps up in dangerousness as we test it&quot; is kind of a well-done trope on the site at this point. If this is missing anything, it's how the various versions of the SCP document are related. I was, for instance, busily trying to memorize D-Class numbers in the anticipation they would turn up again when the shit hit the fan, but that never happened. I'm not sure what exactly goes on to provide the improved understand of the object as time progresses.</p>
<p>Beyond that, the &quot;everything is a dream&quot; finale was&#8230; I mean, it's okay. This is a good visualization of that idea. Maybe it's just that the idea itself isn't terribly fresh. Someone else can probably give you better feedback. :/</p>
<p>Minor notes: &quot;drive&quot; is not the right word for a boat. Shortly after that in the same log is &quot;a vast expanses&quot;. Also, &quot;thaumatergic&quot;.</p>

